# Product-molecularity fixture: one complex A.B.D. The rule deletes A-B and
# creates X bonded to A and D, claiming two products, A.X.D and B. The only D is
# the one bonded to B, which a bimolecular rule may match only with
# block_same_complex_binding=False; D stays bonded to B, so the products do not
# separate and the rule must not fire (Xtot stays 0). Main fired it (Xtot 1).
begin model
begin parameters
  k 1
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A(b,c)
  B(a,d)
  D(e,x)
  X(a,d)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  A(b!1,c).B(a!1,d!2).D(e!2,x) 1
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules Xtot X()
end observables
begin reaction rules
  A(b!1,c).B(a!1) + D(x) -> A(b,c!3).X(a!3,d!4).D(x!4) + B(a) k
end reaction rules
end model
writeXML()
